<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William II, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1365–1417</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as William VI, Count of Holland, William II of Bavaria-Straubing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William II was Duke of Bavaria-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/straubing">Straubing</a> from 1404 to 1417 and, as William VI, Count of Holland, Zeeland and Hainaut. A son of Duke Albert I, he governed mainly from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>, where the Hook and Cod factions divided Holland. His death in 1417 left his only daughter, Jacqueline, as heiress, and her uncle John III contested her inheritance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-ii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="William II, Duke of Bavaria" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numisantica · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Graaf_Holland_Henegouwen_Willem_VI_van_Beieren_dubbele_groot_tuin_Valenciennes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
